\echo 'Test 1.7: a node above the scan reads the aggregate'
Test 1.7: a node above the scan reads the aggregate
EXPLAIN (COSTS OFF, VERBOSE, TIMING OFF)
SELECT DISTINCT account_id, COUNT(*), SUM(price)
FROM pinned_key_items
WHERE account_id = 1 AND id @@@ paradedb.all()
GROUP BY account_id;
                                                                                                                             QUERY PLAN                                                                                                                             
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 HashAggregate
   Output: account_id, (count(*)), (sum(price))
   Group Key: (count(*)), (sum(pinned_key_items.price))
   ->  Custom Scan (ParadeDB Aggregate Scan)
         Output: account_id, (count(*)), (sum(price))
         Backend: DataFusion
         Indexes: pinned_key_items_idx (pinned_key_items)
         Aggregates: COUNT(*), SUM(price)
         DataFusion Physical Plan: 
           : AggregateExec: mode=Single, gby=[true as __one_group], aggr=[count(1) as agg_0, sum(pinned_key_items_0.price) as agg_1, first_value(pinned_key_items_0.account_id) ORDER BY [pinned_key_items_0.ctid_0 ASC NULLS LAST] as row_0], ordering_mode=Sorted
           :   ProjectionExec: expr=[ctid@0 as ctid_0, account_id@1 as account_id, price@2 as price]
           :     CooperativeExec
           :       PgSearchScan: table=pinned_key_items, segments=1, visibility=eager, query={"boolean":{"must":[{"with_index":{"query":"all"}},{"term":{"field":"account_id","value":1}}]}}
(13 rows)

